>> title: Macaroni Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: pasta, mayonnaise, side, no-cook dressing, make-ahead
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: elbow macaroni salad, deli macaroni salad, creamy pasta salad, mac salad
>> pairs-with: mayonnaise, potato-salad, coleslaw
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — pasta left to cool in its own water goes to mush, and no amount of dressing rescues it afterwards

>> step: boil the macaroni 8 min, rinse cold
Boil @elbow macaroni{1%lb}(450 g) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs} and ~boil{8%min}, a minute past al dente, then rinse it cold.

>> step: whisk the dressing
Whisk @mayonnaise{1 1/4%cup}(300 mL), @cider vinegar{3%Tbs}, @granulated sugar{1%Tbs}(12 g), @yellow mustard{1%Tbs}, @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} until it is looser than you think it should be.

>> step: fold in the crunch
Fold @&(~1)dressing{} through @&(~2)cooled macaroni{} with @celery{2%ribs}(diced small), @red bell pepper{1/2}(diced small), @carrot{1%small}(grated) and @yellow onion{1/4%small}(grated).

>> step: chill 2 hr, loosen with milk
Chill @&(~1)macaroni salad{} ~chill{2%hr}, then loosen it with @whole milk{2%Tbs} and taste for salt and vinegar before it goes out.
